drm/imagination: a7a runtime-PM robustness (rebased from the v6.16 graft onto upstream master, 2026-09-09)

Three things upstream master (7.3-rc2) still lacks, all soaked on the A733 with runtime power-down enabled
(docs/OPEN-STACK-WEDGE-2026-09-09.md, "Power fix soak"):
 1. clear fwif_sysinit->firmware_started before every firmware (re)start: the flag lives in the firmware heap
    and survives a runtime power-off, so pvr_wait_for_fw_boot() otherwise returns on the previous life's value;
 2. if pvr_power_fw_disable() fails inside runtime suspend, restart the firmware instead of returning the error
    with the GPU half powered down (runtime PM then believes it is active and every later job "locks up");
 3. a gpu node without a power-domains property gives -ENOENT from of_count_phandle_with_args() and aborted
    the probe; treat it as 0 domains.
Dropped from the v6.16 version: the per-poll pvr_fw_stop() warnings (diagnostic only; master rewrote that
function for RISC-V firmware).

--- a/drivers/gpu/drm/imagination/pvr_power.c
+++ b/drivers/gpu/drm/imagination/pvr_power.c
@@ -126,6 +126,11 @@
 	if (rpm_resume)
 		enable_irq(pvr_dev->irq);
 
+	/* a7a: firmware_started lives in the FW heap and survives a power-off, so without this the
+	 * boot wait below returns on the previous life's value before the restarted firmware has
+	 * actually booted (upstream only clears it once, in pvr_fw_init()). */
+	WRITE_ONCE(pvr_dev->fw_dev.fwif_sysinit->firmware_started, false);
+
 	err = pvr_fw_start(pvr_dev);
 	if (err)
 		goto out;
@@ -380,8 +385,17 @@
 
 	if (READ_ONCE(pvr_dev->fw_dev.initialised)) {
 		err = pvr_power_fw_disable(pvr_dev, false, true);
-		if (err)
+		if (err) {
+			/* a7a: the firmware has already powered its units down when the host's idle polls
+			 * fail; returning the error leaves runtime PM believing the GPU is active while the
+			 * firmware is half dead (every later job "locks up": docs/OPEN-STACK-WEDGE-2026-09-09.md).
+			 * Restart it. pvr_power_fw_disable() re-enables the IRQ itself on its failure path,
+			 * and never disabled it when the idle/power-off requests failed, so rpm_resume is false. */
+			drm_warn(drm_dev, "runtime suspend aborted (%d): restarting the firmware\n", err);
+			if (pvr_power_fw_enable(pvr_dev, false))
+				drm_err(drm_dev, "firmware restart after aborted suspend failed\n");
 			goto err_drm_dev_exit;
+		}
 	}
 
 	err = pvr_dev->device_data->pwr_ops->power_off(pvr_dev);
@@ -635,6 +649,10 @@
 
 	domain_count = of_count_phandle_with_args(dev->of_node, "power-domains",
 						  "#power-domain-cells");
+	/* a7a: a node with NO power-domains property gives -ENOENT here and aborted the probe on the
+	 * A733, whose GPU sits in no described domain; 0 domains need no work (the <= 1 check below). */
+	if (domain_count == -ENOENT)
+		domain_count = 0;
 	if (domain_count < 0) {
 		err = domain_count;
 		goto out;
